# Content-builder parent (integration)

The **parent** Cursor agent is the production manager. Specialists submit against `content-builder/catalogue/contracts/`. Deterministic scripts import, index, build, and check.

**Copywriter owns final wording. Director owns instructional coherence. Engineer implements approved specifications.** Do not have every agent rewrite the lesson.

Onboarding (`catalogue/onboarding/`, `scripts/import_mcf3m_package.py`) must finish before further revision-plan prose, hooks, or interactives. Specialists load `resolved-context.{role}.json` when present.

## Sequence

1. Audit failures when revising (save a fixture). Establish contracts.
2. `lesson-director` → `lesson-brief.json`
3. **Parallel:** `practice-designer`, `hook-curator`, `visual-experience-designer`, writing-model comparison (parent picks copywriter model)
4. `interaction-designer` **and** `formative-feedback-designer` (joint contract)
5. `student-copywriter` → `student-content.json`
6. `lesson-engineer` (+ visual CSS already in components) compiles static HTML (worktree if shared `components/`)
7. `lesson-verifier` independently; parent saves the report
8. Parent resolves findings; present before/after to Shawn

Do **not** invoke these specialists for LMS, Drive banks, MnCi decks, or Attendance & Participation.

Superseded names (do not start new lessons with these): `curriculum-mapper` → director; `question-curator` → practice-designer; `instruction-author` → copywriter.

## Worktrees

When two writers would edit the same files:

```bash
content-builder/scripts/isolated-worktree.sh {agent} {lesson_id}
```

Copy **only** `content-builder/` paths back. Leave uncommitted `lms/` files in the primary checkout untouched. Specialists never `git merge`.

## Durable corrections

Every accepted Shawn correction updates the relevant rule, writer-reference exemplar, component, or test. Preserve locks; show conflicts when a shared change would overwrite locked content.
